  "source_afterbinding": {
    "id": "def-arakawa-suzuki-casimir-operators-on-tensor-functors",
    "current_raw_sha256": "55d22007b6a69dc8a5f7322dca63e7badcdf6ef95aeedcc56bc0f3555a6474bc",
    "exact_reviewed_proposal": {
      "path": "research/frontier-44-special-representation-examples-28-owner-greeting-recovery-20261011/owner-creation-afterbinding/proposals/def-arakawa-suzuki-casimir-operators-on-tensor-functors.F2-only.md",
      "sha256": "55d22007b6a69dc8a5f7322dca63e7badcdf6ef95aeedcc56bc0f3555a6474bc"
    },
    "actual_F2": "[F2] The Casimir tensor $\\Omega=\\sum_{ij}E_{ij}\\otimes E_{ji}\\in U(\\mathfrak g)\\otimes U(\\mathfrak g)$ is independent of dual bases and invariant under the diagonal adjoint action: $[X\\otimes1+1\\otimes X,\\Omega]=0$ for every $X\\in\\mathfrak g$. Indeed, for $X=E_{ab}$ the matrix-unit relations give the cancelling sum $\\sum_jE_{aj}\\otimes E_{jb}-\\sum_iE_{ib}\\otimes E_{ai}+\\sum_iE_{ib}\\otimes E_{ai}-\\sum_jE_{aj}\\otimes E_{jb}=0$, and linearity gives every $X$. Therefore its action on a tensor product of $\\mathfrak g$-modules is a $\\mathfrak g$-intertwiner. Module actions extend uniquely to $U(\\mathfrak g)$ ([[def-casimir-operator-relative-to-an-invariant-form]], [[lem-the-casimir-operator-is-basis-independent-and-intertwining]], [[lem-the-casimir-element-is-independent-of-dual-bases]], [[def-universal-enveloping-algebra]]).",
    "actual_source_exactly_matches_inspected_F2_only_proposal": true,
    "Statement_Definition_proof_and_other_metadata_unchanged": true,
    "actual_necessary_use_rechecked": [
      "Proof1.2 uses exactly tensor-product intertwining from the displayed diagonal matrix-unit cancellation; module-map naturality follows from the explicit sum of representation operators",
